{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794304602,"nonce":"MTo+wTeD0z67ZRHOwk5B83O4imM=","title":"No h-adaptivity that keeps a structured lattice","message":"On a shape.structured() domain h-adaptive remeshing refuses by name, and the only way to refine is to change sizes by hand. Options: rebuild the rectilinear lattice with each slab's spacing taken from the marked size field (a slab takes the finest size along it, so refinement spreads along whole slabs), or local splitting with hanging nodes on .structured().quad() lattices (jno.solve.refine exists for quads and hexes). Tet lattices have no lattice-preserving split.","files":null}]}